### Route definition (orchestration YAML)
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — declares the linear pipeline (each step's `next` chains to the following one, all under a `transaction` governance, authorized by `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`):

```
validate → normalize → unique → household → email → build → household-assign → registrationDate → customerCode → save → respond
```

Mapping of steps to classes (all in package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner`):

| Step | Class |
|------|-------|
| validate | ValidateOwnerFields |
| normalize | NormalizeOwnerTelephone |
| unique | EnsureUniqueTelephone |
| household | EnsureUniqueHousehold |
| email | NormalizeOwnerEmail |
| build | BuildOwner |
| household-assign | AssignHousehold |
| registrationDate | DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate |
| customerCode | AssignCustomerCode |
| save | SaveOwner |
| respond | RespondWithOwnerCreated |

Note: the `owners.POST.yml` sits directly in `.../rest/api/`. The `.../rest/api/owners/` subdirectory holds the OTHER owner routes ({ownerId}.GET/PUT/DELETE, pets, visits), not the POST.

### Pipeline Java classes (full contents)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ValidateOwnerFields.java` — first step. Rejects missing/blank `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone` with `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). Publishes validated body via `Out<OwnerFieldsDto>` so later steps use `@Val` (they must not re-bind `@RequestBody`).
```java
public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated)
        throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
    List<String> missing = new ArrayList<>();
    require("firstName", request.getFirstName(), missing);
    require("lastName", request.getLastName(), missing);
    require("address", request.getAddress(), missing);
    require("city", request.getCity(), missing);
    require("telephone", request.getTelephone(), missing);
    if (!missing.isEmpty()) { throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing); }
    validated.set(request);
}
private static void require(String name, String value, List<String> missing) {
    if (value == null || value.isBlank()) { missing.add(name); }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java` — mutates telephone into E.164 (strips spaces/dashes/brackets; `+` keeps country code else assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`; must be 8–15 digits or throws `InvalidTelephoneException`).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueTelephone.java` — rejects a normalized telephone already used by any existing owner with `DuplicateTelephoneException` (409).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueHousehold.java` — the household duplicate-detection step (details in section 3).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/NormalizeOwnerEmail.java` — email optional; validates + lower-cases via `OwnerEmails.normalize`, else `InvalidEmailException` (400).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerEmails.java` — shared helper (not a function class), regex `^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java` — maps DTO to `Owner` via `OwnerMapper.toOwner(request)`, publishes `Out<Owner>`.
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built) {
    built.set(ownerMapper.toOwner(request));
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java` — stamps the shared household id onto the built owner (details in section 3).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java` — defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when absent.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` — sets `customerCode` = `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (first 3 letters of last name upper-cased; sequence = owner count + 1, zero-padded to 4).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/SaveOwner.java` — `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` — maps to `OwnerDto`, responds `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.

Note on `ApplyOwner.java` (same package): it exists but is NOT wired into the POST pipeline (BuildOwner uses the mapper instead). It re-applies fields including `OwnerEmails.normalize`. Likely legacy/unused by this route.

### Related escalation handlers (each has a matching `.yml` in `.../officefloor/escalation/`)
- `MissingOwnerFieldsExceptionHandler` → 400, body `{"errors":[<field names>]}`
- `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler` → 409, body `{"errors":["telephone"]}`
- `DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler` → 409, body `{"errors":["household"]}`
- Plus `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler`, `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`, and generic handlers (`GeneralExceptionHandler`, `ValidationExceptionHandler`, `NotFoundExceptionHandler`, etc.)

Escalation wiring example — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateHouseholdException.yml`:
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler
```

## 2. Owner entity & where `address` is defined/validated

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — JPA entity `@Table(name="owners")`, extends `Person`. The `address` field:
```java
@Column(name = "address")
@NotEmpty
private String address;
```
Important: the entity uses `@NotEmpty` (jakarta.validation), NOT `@NotBlank`. Other fields: `city` (`@NotEmpty`), `telephone` (`@NotEmpty` + `@Pattern ^\+[0-9]{8,15}$`), plus `email`, `registrationDate`, `customerCode`, and `householdId` (`@Column(name="household_id")`, no validation annotation). Bean-validation on the entity is generally not what enforces create-time address presence — that is done explicitly in `ValidateOwnerFields` (`isBlank()` check), which produces the 400 with a named-field body.

### Request DTO (generated, not in `src`)
`OwnerFieldsDto` is generated at build time by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin into `target/generated-sources/openapi/...` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, `modelNameSuffix=Dto`). Its schema lives in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (schema `OwnerFields`, around lines 2000–2064). The `address` schema:
```yaml
address:
  title: Address
  description: The postal address of the pet owner.
  type: string
  minLength: 1
  maxLength: 255
  example: '110 W. Liberty St.'
```
`OwnerFields.required` lists `firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone`. The write-only `sharesHousehold` boolean is defined at lines 2051–2058. The read-only `householdId` is on the `Owner` schema (lines 2100–2107).

## 3. Household duplicate-detection & shared-household-id logic

This is the core of what you asked about. Three classes:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueHousehold.java` (full logic):
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository,
        Out<HouseholdId> householdIdOut) throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
    String lastName = canonical(request.getLastName());
    String address = canonical(request.getAddress());

    List<Owner> matches = new ArrayList<>();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (lastName.equals(canonical(existing.getLastName()))
                && address.equals(canonical(existing.getAddress()))) {
            matches.add(existing);
        }
    }

    if (matches.isEmpty()) {
        householdIdOut.set(null); // unique household — nothing to share
        return;
    }

    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
    }

    // Caller opted into sharing: give this owner and every match the same stable identifier.
    String householdId = deriveHouseholdId(lastName, address);
    for (Owner match : matches) {
        if (match.getHouseholdId() == null) {
            match.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(match);
        }
    }
    householdIdOut.set(new HouseholdId(householdId));
}

private static String deriveHouseholdId(String canonicalLastName, String canonicalAddress) {
    String seed = "household:" + canonicalLastName + "|" + canonicalAddress;
    return UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes(seed.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)).toString();
}

private static String canonical(String value) {
    if (value == null) { return ""; }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase();
}
```
Key behaviors:
- Duplicate = same `lastName` AND `address`, compared via `canonical()`: trim, collapse internal whitespace runs to a single space, lower-case.
- If a match exists and `sharesHousehold` is not true → `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).
- If `sharesHousehold` is true → derives a stable `householdId` = `UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes("household:<canonLastName>|<canonAddress>")` (a deterministic type-3 name UUID), back-fills it onto matching existing owners lacking one, and publishes it downstream.
- No match → publishes `null` (no household to share).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/HouseholdId.java` — a tiny wrapper type carrying the id from EnsureUniqueHousehold to AssignHousehold (a dedicated type so OfficeFloor by-type variable matching is unambiguous vs a raw String). `value()` returns the String (may be null).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java`:
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val HouseholdId householdId) {
    if (householdId != null && householdId.value() != null) {
        owner.setHouseholdId(householdId.value());
    }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdException.java` — carries `lastName` + `address`, message `"Household already registered for lastName '...' at address '...'"`.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateHouseholdExceptionHandler.java` — responds `409 CONFLICT`, body `{"errors":["household"]}`.

### Load-bearing observation (likely relevant to your task)
The current `canonical()` normalization only trims, collapses whitespace, and lower-cases. It does NOT expand street-type abbreviations. But the two household tests (below) use `"12 Main St"` vs `"12 main street"` and expect them to be treated as the SAME address. Under the current code `canonical("12 Main St")` = `"12 main st"` and `canonical("12  main  street")` = `"12 main street"`, which are NOT equal — so as written those tests would currently fail (Cp10 expects 409 conflict; Cp11 expects a shared householdId). Implementing `St`↔`Street` (abbreviation) normalization in `canonical()` appears to be the intended change.

## 4. Tests related to owner creation / address / household

All acceptance tests live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/` (`Cp01Tests.java` … `Cp12Tests.java`, plus `AcceptanceBase.java` and `AuditLogCapture.java`). Every checkpoint exercises `POST /api/owners`. Only Cp10 and Cp11 reference `household`:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/Cp10Tests.java` (household-duplicate; `@Tag("cp10")`):
```java
@Test
void coreRejectsAddressesThatNormalizeEqual() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode a = ownerNode(); a.put("address", "12 Main St");
    createOwnerOk(a);
    ObjectNode b = ownerNode(); b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
    b.put("address", "12  main  street");
    createOwner(b).andExpect(status().isConflict());
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/Cp11Tests.java` (shares-household; `@Tag("cp11")`):
```java
@Test
void coreSameHouseholdIdForNormalizedEqualAddresses() throws Exception {
    ObjectNode a = ownerNode(); a.put("address", "12 Main St");
    createOwnerOk(a);
    ObjectNode b = ownerNode(); b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
    b.put("address", "12 main street"); b.put("sharesHousehold", true);
    int idb = createOwnerOk(b);
    ObjectNode c = ownerNode(); c.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
    c.put("address", "12  MAIN  ST"); c.put("sharesHousehold", true);
    int idc = createOwnerOk(c);
    assertEquals(fetchOwner(idb).get("householdId").asText(),
                 fetchOwner(idc).get("householdId").asText());
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the shared harness (full contents read). Key facts: `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional` (each test rolls back), `@WithMockUser(roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`. Helpers used by the household tests: `ownerNode()` (fully-unique valid payload: firstName "Test", unique lastName/address/city/telephone), `createOwner(body)` (POST /api/owners), `createOwnerOk(body)` (asserts 2xx, returns id), `fetchOwner(id)` (GET /api/owners/{id}, returns JsonNode). Uses Jackson `tools.jackson.databind` (Jackson 3).

## 5. Build system & running tests

Build system: Maven. `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` — artifactId `spring-petclinic-rest`, parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`. Key deps: `net.officefloor.springboot:officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter`, `net.officefloor.web:woof_test` (test), spring-boot-starter-webmvc / data-jpa / security / validation, H2/HSQLDB (test/runtime DBs), MapStruct (processor), and the openapi-generator + build-helper plugins that generate the `...rest.dto` / `...rest.api` sources into `target/generated-sources/openapi/` at build time.

Maven wrapper present: `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`).

Run tests (from repo root `/home/daniel/sandbox`):
- Full build + tests: `./mvnw test`
- Single household test class: `./mvnw test -Dtest=Cp11Tests` (or `Cp10Tests`)
- The tests are JUnit 5 tagged (`@Tag("cp10")`, `@Tag("cp11")`, …); the pom's surefire config was not explicitly shown enabling tag filtering, so run by class name with `-Dtest=` for reliability. Because DTO sources are generated, run through Maven (not a bare `javac`) so `generate-sources` runs first.

Docs: `/home/daniel/sandbox/CLAUDE.md` and `/home/daniel/sandbox/AGENTS.md` exist at the repo root and may contain project-specific conventions if you need more context.

